{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase","id":1039286,"title":"[CofD Rulebook] Social Chase","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-27T23:57:57-08:00","id":1039286,"title":"[CofD Rulebook] Social Chase","content":"I plan to run jury trial scene ( Consilium trial on Scelesti from <b>Mage</b> game to be precise ) with one of PCs working as defensive advocate of accused ( factotum ). I think that trying to win judges or jury would be great example of Social Chase mechanics between two advocates. Only I do have a problem with Setting a Terms for the trial - Who would start? What would be good Circumstances modifiers? Any help will be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-28-2017, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T03:34:53-08:00","id":1039338,"title":"","content":"For now, I have something like this for Trial as Social Chase. Defendant ( or his advocate ) and prosecutor are sides in the Chase. Each cross-examination is one turn of Chase, Edge has the side that is calling witness or evidence. After each calling of witness or evidence, Required Successes should be checked if they do not change. Short counsel between lawyers of the sides ( and their assistances, helps and defendant ) are treated as Teamwork action, with advocate question/speech on witness as Primary Actor roll. If one side of Social Chase get\u2019s all Required Successes, trial is ending and each side has last chance to swing her winning by final speech \u2013 they make last roll ( probably based on Manipulation or Intelligence, Politics or Expression ) and those success are added to their Required Successes. Side with most success, wins trial and her goal about Defendant is resolution \u2013 or closest possible to it.<br /> <br /> And here is Required Successes Modifiers table I made. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Social Chase ( Trial ) Modifiers</b></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Circumstance</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Modifier</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One judge is initially against your goal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2 (Each)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One judge is initially in favor of your goal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-2 (Each)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Evidence or Testimony is against your goal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1 (Each)</td> </tr> </table></div> Any comments on those rules or Modifiers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:11:45-08:00","id":1039355,"title":"","content":"The Edge goes to whomever gets to speak first, I would say. How are you organizing your trial? Do the prosecuters get to open up the case first? Or does the defendant? I'm personally leaning towards prosecuters, because they get to go on the &quot;attack.&quot; They get to choose the grounds to fight in. They're the ones being proactive, and the defnese re-active.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for modifiers*... While I get where you're coming from, but each of those modifiers is entirely in the hands of the ST, and not the players. If you look at the Chase modifiers, its all about who has the higher initiative, who's got the higher speed, who is smaller (ie wolf form), can't be tired out (vampire body), etc. Chases are further modified by things like Fleet of Foot and Parkour. Nearly all things found on a character sheet. The only one NOT on a character sheet is &quot;Dangerous Environment.&quot; A +1 through +3, depending on ST. That's the modifier that should apply. Well, &quot;know the territory&quot; can also reflect knowing the judges, so I could suggest basing that on sympathetic connection to the judges, perhaps,which is a similar thing.<br /> <br /> I would suggest using things like Status, Mentor, social skills, Doors / Impression and the like. Replace the Chase's initiative modifiers with Impression. Someone has a better impression, the opponent gets +1 for each step they are better (ie a three impression difference is +3). Number of Doors would replace Speed modifiers, though I would replace the +5 modifier with 5x Doors instead of 10x. Social Merits, such Sympathetic or Fast Talking that open Doors should work like Parkour and reduce the necessary target number by the appropriate amount. Status serves as a social bonus as normal (equivalent to Fleet of Foot). Though you'll have to figure out how to handle Order Status if the judges are mixed Orders, or just go with City Status.<br /> <br /> I recommend using &quot;Evidence and Testimony&quot; run as Clues that can be used to give the each side modifiers to their goal. Each side will be giving evidence and testimony, sometimes new testimonies given on the fly in responce to something else, so having it modify the initial goal is a bit strange. This way its a bit more flexible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * You're having each judge count twice. Once in favor of your goal, and once in opposition of the opponet's goal. So, if there was one judge and she was predisposed to the prosecution, the prosecuter would have -2 while the defense would get +2, for a total of +4 difference. That's a bit excessive if there's an odd number of judges, and makes everything a bit too weighted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:30:11-08:00","id":1039361,"title":"","content":"Also, you might want to tweak the target number. I've personally found that a TN of 5 isn't nearly dramatic enough when dealing with characters built for a chase. Even if all involved are. Two rolls ends things way too fast for my tastes, and leaves things up to chance of a lucky roll or not far more than it should. I've seen characters succeed on Chases that they should have, for all intents and purposes, miserably failed, simply due to a very lucky first roll with crap dice. While you can argue that's keeping with the spirit of the rules, it was rather anti-climatic for something that was supposed to be a big plot point. Its <i>fun </i>to fight over who's got the Edge, and chase to who gets to the TN first. Being over too fast is boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:36:26-08:00","id":1039363,"title":"","content":"As for the Edge? I recommend that, past the first turn, you just have a Wits + Empathy face off. How well you can read the room determines who gets the Edge. Or forget the prosecuter starts with edge and do that roll for each turn. Your call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:01:53-08:00","id":1039370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039355#post1039355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Edge goes to whomever gets to speak first, I would say. How are you organizing your trial? Do the prosecuters get to open up the case first? Or does the defendant? I'm personally leaning towards prosecuters, because they get to go on the &quot;attack.&quot; They get to choose the grounds to fight in. They're the ones being proactive, and the defnese re-active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed here, it was prosecution that always start trial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039355#post1039355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for modifiers*... While I get where you're coming from, but each of those modifiers is entirely in the hands of the ST, and not the players. If you look at the Chase modifiers, its all about who has the higher initiative, who's got the higher speed, who is smaller (ie wolf form), can't be tired out (vampire body), etc. Chases are further modified by things like Fleet of Foot and Parkour. Nearly all things found on a character sheet. The only one NOT on a character sheet is &quot;Dangerous Environment.&quot; A +1 through +3, depending on ST. That's the modifier that should apply. Well, &quot;know the territory&quot; can also reflect knowing the judges, so I could suggest basing that on sympathetic connection to the judges, perhaps,which is a similar thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will asses this in the moment, but I do not see very much Skills implying winning the Trial. It's <b>all</b> about social environment. Your Skills and such <i>can</i> help you made argument ( and collect success needed to get ), but main deciding factor is much more stance of society on things the trial is touching than how good you are with your words. Law, not how weasel you are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039355#post1039355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest using things like Status, Mentor, social skills, Doors / Impression and the like. Replace the Chase's initiative modifiers with Impression. Someone has a better impression, the opponent gets +1 for each step they are better (ie a three impression difference is +3).</div> </div> </div> </div>Impressions are still all the ST thing. You change ax for stick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039355#post1039355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Number of Doors would replace Speed modifiers, though I would replace the +5 modifier with 5x Doors instead of 10x. Social Merits, such Sympathetic or Fast Talking that open Doors should work like Parkour and reduce the necessary target number by the appropriate amount. Status serves as a social bonus as normal (equivalent to Fleet of Foot).</div> </div> </div> </div>Doors to who? I need to count Door for each judge superatlety? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In Consilium trial, with only few judges it will be problematic and needless math. In mortal typical jury process, with two dozen of 'judges'? Uncountable. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039355#post1039355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though you'll have to figure out how to handle Order Status if the judges are mixed Orders, or just go with City Status.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what City Status? Difference between lawyers and each judge?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039355#post1039355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend using &quot;Evidence and Testimony&quot; run as Clues that can be used to give the each side modifiers to their goal. Each side will be giving evidence and testimony, sometimes new testimonies given on the fly in responce to something else, so having it modify the initial goal is a bit strange. This way its a bit more flexible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using &quot;Evidence and Testimony&quot; as Clues would mean they just gives +1 bonus to one cross-examination roll. With Dicepools like 6-8 for professional lawyers, those will be not very 'game changing', which is contrary stempl of court drama genere. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think that moving Required Success a bit is enough change to make really change in the Chase, i.e. really worthwhile to look for Evidence and Testimonies in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039355#post1039355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* You're having each judge count twice. Once in favor of your goal, and once in opposition of the opponet's goal. So, if there was one judge and she was predisposed to the prosecution, the prosecuter would have -2 while the defense would get +2, for a total of +4 difference. That's a bit excessive if there's an odd number of judges, and makes everything a bit too weighted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here is good point, probably. Let's just check it on my sample London Consilium and players trying to stop death of mages, large portion of Diamond society want's dead. There are 7 Councilors judges ( with Hierarch counted in it ). Four of them start with wanting to kill Defendants. Two want to save them. One is undecided. For players wanting to save Defendants it would mean 4*(+2) + 2*(-2) = +4 to Required Success on start. To persecution going after kill it would be 4*(-2) + 2*(+2) = -4 to Required Success on start.<br /> <br /> So yes, difference is <i>enourmous </i>in my initial proposition. I will probably leave only +1 for the judge not agreeing to your goal. This way our players would have only +4 to Required Success on start and persecution will have +2 to Required Success, making trial much more even. And &quot;Evidence and Testimony&quot; change of Required Success would mean ever more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:08:01-08:00","id":1039373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039363#post1039363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Edge? I recommend that, past the first turn, you just have a Wits + Empathy face off. How well you can read the room determines who gets the Edge. Or forget the prosecuter starts with edge and do that roll for each turn. Your call.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good advice here, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:40:15-08:00","id":1039382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039361#post1039361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you might want to tweak the target number. I've personally found that a TN of 5 isn't nearly dramatic enough when dealing with characters built for a chase. Even if all involved are. Two rolls ends things way too fast for my tastes, and leaves things up to chance of a lucky roll or not far more than it should. I've seen characters succeed on Chases that they should have, for all intents and purposes, miserably failed, simply due to a very lucky first roll with crap dice. While you can argue that's keeping with the spirit of the rules, it was rather anti-climatic for something that was supposed to be a big plot point. Its <i>fun </i>to fight over who's got the Edge, and chase to who gets to the TN first. Being over too fast is boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, maybe add + 1 Required Success for each judge in general also. In our example with Consilium it would be +7 Required Success for each side, and in mortal U.S. court it would be like +20 Required Success for each side, because of jury. Not strange that those legal cases in modern democracies take soooo long then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:43:09-08:00","id":1039384,"title":"","content":"New version of Modifiers table...<br /> <br /> <b>Social Chase ( Trial ) Modifiers</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><i>Circumstance </i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><i>Modifier</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Number of judges</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">+1 (Each)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">One judge is initially against your goal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">+1 (Each)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Evidence or Testimony is against your goal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">+1 (Each)</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:49:10-08:00","id":1039387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1039286-cofd-rulebook-social-chase?p=1039370#post1039370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will asses this in the moment, but I do not see very much Skills implying winning the Trial. It's all about social enviorment. Your Skills and such <i>can</i> help you made argument ( and collect success needed ), but main deciding is much more stance of society on things the trial is touching than how good you are with your words. Law, not how weasel you are.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, you do what's best for your game, but everything I'm telling you is based on my personal experiences with using the rules. I've found that using more things on character sheets is more engaging for players than less, and encourages them to spread out their abilities for future incidents. YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Impressions are still all the ST thing. You change ax for stick. </div> </div> </div> Its something that players have some amount of control over, especially in the form of spells and merits. So, I'm going to have to disagree with you on that one based on my personal experience. If it doesn't apply to your game, then *shrugs* Don't know what to tell you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doors to who? </div> </div> </div> Everyone at once. We're not social maneuvering, we're translating abilities from one subsystem to another. This is how I'm recommending translating abilities. If you could use Sympathetic to open two Doors, for Social Chases you instead get an ability that grants two free auto-successes towards your target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what City Status? </div> </div> </div> Whatever city this trial is in. Generally speaking, mages would hold trial in front of the reigning Consilium, one from each Path if dealing with a major issue. While Orders are global, Consilium are city-based, laws broken are generally tried at city level. If you're going before a Conclave, that's generally Silver Ladder (the only big game in town), so just use Silver Ladder Status instead.<br /> <br /> If you're doing something different *shrugs* I'm just rattling off suggestions here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using &quot;Evidence and Testimony&quot; as Clues would mean they just gives +1 bonus to one cross-examination roll. With Dicepools like 6-8 for profesional laywers, those will be not very 'game changing', which is contrary stample of court drama genere. </div> </div> </div> Umm.... I'm afraid you're slightly incorrect here.<br /> <br /> Clues can go up to +3 dice with experts and exceptional successes. Which, given players gathering them, happens with high frequency. A mage with four dots in Occult and the Inspired Condition from Fate can easily net that +3 bonus when gathering info or serving as expert testimony. You can also spend multiple Clues on a single roll, netting you over a +5 bonus; clues are specifically exempt from the +5 limit. Three clues with +3 each can easily yield a +9 dice bonus on a single roll.<br /> <br /> To use Pheonix Wright styles games as an inspiration for a moment (because I admittedly do that with my games), basically what happens is that you do Investigation before the trial, gather up Clues, execute them through rolls right away, then go out and gather more Clues during trial breaks. Or I've also used DtD-style &quot;retroactive preparation&quot; that they recommend for heists. Make a roll before the trial, then you can do a flashback montage of gathering evidence a number of times equal to successes rolled.<br /> <br /> Again, if you have something different in mind, then my suggestions won't work. But tha'ts what I've done before to good effect. Take it as you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T07:21:55-08:00","id":1039411,"title":"","conte